<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-10-08.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="003852"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#003852" label="[00:38:52]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">( I may be looking into 8bit ROM creation for inspiration )</span></div><div class="line" id="065528"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#065528" label="[06:55:28]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Tiny C Compiler is relicensing to MIT <a rel="nofollow" href="https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git/blob/3d963aebcd533da278f086a3e559d24b961e8c31:/RELICENSING">https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git/blob/3d963aebcd533da278f086a3e559d24b961e8c31:/RELICENSING</a>  <a rel="nofollow" href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=41763624">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=41763624</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="193520"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#193520" label="[19:35:20]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">pabs3: probably trying to go the clang route of getting corporate support (unlikely and honestly would probably result in a total rewrite as the TCC source code is an absolute tangled mess)</span></div><div class="line" id="211512"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#211512" label="[21:15:12]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Kind of doubt it would require much of a rewrite given how that file is 10+ years old and Fabrice Bellard agrees on relicensing his code: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git/history/3d963aebcd533da278f086a3e559d24b961e8c31:/RELICENSING">https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git/history/3d963aebcd533da278f086a3e559d24b961e8c31:/RELICENSING</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="213356"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#213356" label="[21:33:56]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">That said the mob thing makes me wonder if it could ever be relicensed</span></div><div class="line" id="215144"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#215144" label="[21:51:44]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">lanodan: the rewrite comment was not about copyright but about the level of clarity in the existing code (which is a rat's nest of accumulation)</span></div><br /></div></body></html>